Part (a): Derive the following First-Order Energy Corrections relation from the preceding result, showing the algebra, calculus, counting, or physical identity used at each step.
\[
\begin{aligned}
E_n^{(1)}
&=\frac{2F}{L}\int_0^L x\sin^2\left(\frac{n\pi x}{L}\right)dx\\
&=\frac{F}{L}\int_0^L x\left[1-\cos\left(\frac{2n\pi x}{L}\right)\right]dx\\
&=\frac{F}{L}\left(\frac{L^2}{2}-0\right)=\frac{FL}{2}.
\end{aligned}
\tag*{[6]}
\]

